# A FALSE REPAIR: the reconciler agreed with itself. Found and fixed 2026-10-02.
#
# This is kept as a pin because it is the most instructive failure in this
# repo, and because the fix is the only thing that makes `reconcile()` safe.
#
# THE BUG. The first version of reconcile() found commits carrying
# `Dispatch-Id:` by scanning `git rev-list --all`, and recorded COMMIT for each
# one it found. `--all` includes the LOCAL WORKTREE. So a commit the Worker had
# made and never pushed — the exact window the whole design exists to cover —
# was recorded as delivered.
#
# MEASURED, from the `commit` row of the crash matrix:
#     remote refs : c6b7195 refs/heads/main
#     local  HEAD : 0bdb34c            <- a different object
#     ledger said : COMMIT @ 0bdb34c
#     cold clone  : `git cat-file -e 0bdb34c` -> NO
# A fresh clone of the remote could not see the object the ledger certified.
# The reconciler was not verifying delivery; it was asking the agent whether it
# had done the work, and the agent said yes.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS MORE THAN A CRASH. A hole in a hash chain is visible. This was
# not a hole — it was a VALID ledger with a FALSE entry, which is strictly worse
# than an absence, because absence is at least honest. It is the same shape as
# the fleet's standing failure one level up: a chain that agrees with itself.
# A receipt that re-hashes the system's own output is circular.
#
# THE FIX (src/cell.js, reconcile()). Evidence of delivery must come from a
# witness the reconciler does not control:
#     1. `git ls-remote origin` for the set of tips a stranger could fetch
#     2. a direct `git fetch <remote> <sha>` probe for anything not obviously there
#     3. if neither reaches the remote -> record LOST, a NEGATIVE receipt
# `git log --all` and `git rev-list --all` are still used to enumerate
# candidates, but a candidate is not a finding.
#
# THE REGRESSION TEST: tests/invariants.mjs I11a–I11d, which build the unpushed
# case, ask a COLD CLONE whether the object is visible, and require LOST.
# tests/mutation.mjs mutant B re-introduces the original bug and is killed by
# I11b/I11c. The mutant is the receipt; the test is the claim.
